<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Taehak</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">372</span> · <a href="/centuries/4th-century">4th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Taehak was the national Confucian academy of the Korean kingdom of Goguryeo, founded in 372 under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sosurim-of-goguryeo">King Sosurim</a>. It taught the Chinese classics and history to the sons of the aristocracy and is regarded as the first formal educational institution in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/korea">Korea</a>. Its founding, in the same year that <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/buddhism">Buddhism</a> was received from the Former <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qin-dynasty">Qin</a>, was part of Sosurim's centralising reforms.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/taehak.jpg" alt="Taehak" width="320" height="180" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: GN Coordinator · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Myeongnyundang.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
